{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a74a4241395fd5e4", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Moshi: a speech-text foundation model for real-time dialogue\narXiv: 2410.00037\nAuthors: Alexandre Défossez, Laurent Mazaré, Manu Orsini, Amélie Royer, Patrick Pérez, Hervé Jégou, Edouard Grave, Neil Zeghidour\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: dialogue_system\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present Helium, a 7B-parameter text LLM pre-trained on 2.1T tokens of filtered public English data.\n  2. We train Mimi, a neural audio codec that distills semantic information into the first level of acoustic tokens using a split residual vector quantizer.\n  3. We propose a new hierarchical, streaming architecture for audio language modeling that extends the RQ-Transformer with per-codebook parameters and acoustic delays to jointly generate semantic and acoustic tokens.\n  4. We introduce a multi-stream audio language model architecture that explicitly processes the input and output audio streams in parallel to handle full-duplex dialogues with arbitrary conversational dynamics.\n  5. We introduce Inner Monologue, a training and inference method that predicts time-aligned text tokens as a prefix to audio tokens to significantly improve the linguistic quality of generated speech while remaining compatible with streaming inference.\n  6. We demonstrate that adjusting the delay between text and audio tokens within the Inner Monologue framework allows a single model to function as both a streaming ASR and a streaming TTS system.\n\nTags: LALM, 压缩, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/音频标记-融合, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-混合, TTS/功能-流式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "76c6e56c-0afb-448b-9686-315b09104bea", "uuid": "53f457d7-ccfe-49ef-9e5e-9c958c6a0907", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T16:15:10.175Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Moshi: a speech-text foundation model for real-time dialogue\narXiv: 2410.00037\nAuthors: Alexandre Défossez, Laurent Mazaré, Manu Orsini, Amélie Royer, Patrick Pérez, Hervé Jégou, Edouard Grave, Neil Zeghidour\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: dialogue_system\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present Helium, a 7B-parameter text LLM pre-trained on 2.1T tokens of filtered public English data.\n  2. We train Mimi, a neural audio codec that distills semantic information into the first level of acoustic tokens using a split residual vector quantizer.\n  3. We propose a new hierarchical, streaming architecture for audio language modeling that extends the RQ-Transformer with per-codebook parameters and acoustic delays to jointly generate semantic and acoustic tokens.\n  4. We introduce a multi-stream audio language model architecture that explicitly processes the input and output audio streams in parallel to handle full-duplex dialogues with arbitrary conversational dynamics.\n  5. We introduce Inner Monologue, a training and inference method that predicts time-aligned text tokens as a prefix to audio tokens to significantly improve the linguistic quality of generated speech while remaining compatible with streaming inference.\n  6. We demonstrate that adjusting the delay between text and audio tokens within the Inner Monologue framework allows a single model to function as both a streaming ASR and a streaming TTS system.\n\nTags: LALM, 压缩, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/音频标记-融合, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-混合, TTS/功能-流式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9606fc4caafbe485", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Qwen3-Omni Technical Report\narXiv: 2509.17765\nAuthors: Jin Xu, Zhifang Guo, Hangrui Hu, Yunfei Chu, Xiong Wang, Jinzheng He, Yuxuan Wang, Xian Shi, Ting He, Xinfa Zhu, Yuanjun Lv, Yongqi Wang, Dake Guo, He Wang, Linhan Ma, Pei Zhang, Xinyu Zhang, Hongkun Hao, Zishan Guo, Baosong Yang, Bin Zhang, Ziyang Ma, Xipin Wei, Shuai Bai, Keqin Chen, Xuejing Liu, Peng Wang, Mingkun Yang, Dayiheng Liu, Xingzhang Ren, Bo Zheng, Rui Men, Fan Zhou, Bowen Yu, Jianxin Yang, Le Yu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Qwen3-Omni is the first single multimodal model to maintain state-of-the-art performance across text, image, audio, and video without degradation relative to single-modal counterparts.\n  2. The model adopts a Thinker-Talker Mixture-of-Experts architecture that unifies perception and generation across text, images, audio, and video to yield fluent text and natural real-time speech.\n  3. It replaces the Whisper audio encoder with an Audio Transformer encoder trained from scratch on 20 million hours of supervised audio to yield stronger general-purpose audio representations.\n  4. A multi-codebook autoregressive scheme with a multi-token prediction module is introduced for speech generation, replacing block-wise diffusion with a lightweight causal ConvNet.\n  5. The system supports text interaction in 119 languages, speech understanding in 19 languages, and speech generation in 10 languages.\n  6. A Time-aligned Multimodal Rotary Position Embedding interleaves rotary angles across temporal, height, and width dimensions to enhance long-range dependency modeling for multimodal streams.\n  7. A Thinking model is introduced to explicitly reason over inputs from any modality, including audio-video and audio-only scenarios.\n  8. Qwen3-Omni-30B-A3B-Captioner is fine-tuned to produce detailed, low-hallucination captions for arbitrary audio inputs to address the lack of general-purpose audio captioning models.\n  9. The model achieves a theoretical end-to-end first-packet latency of 234 ms in cold-start settings through chunked prefilling and streaming multi-codebook codec generation.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/对话型, LALM/潜在表示, LALM/对话型-并行生成, TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "76c6e56c-0afb-448b-9686-315b09104bea", "uuid": "36fd85bb-4722-4dfd-bde0-8b8086722111", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T16:15:10.558Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Qwen3-Omni Technical Report\narXiv: 2509.17765\nAuthors: Jin Xu, Zhifang Guo, Hangrui Hu, Yunfei Chu, Xiong Wang, Jinzheng He, Yuxuan Wang, Xian Shi, Ting He, Xinfa Zhu, Yuanjun Lv, Yongqi Wang, Dake Guo, He Wang, Linhan Ma, Pei Zhang, Xinyu Zhang, Hongkun Hao, Zishan Guo, Baosong Yang, Bin Zhang, Ziyang Ma, Xipin Wei, Shuai Bai, Keqin Chen, Xuejing Liu, Peng Wang, Mingkun Yang, Dayiheng Liu, Xingzhang Ren, Bo Zheng, Rui Men, Fan Zhou, Bowen Yu, Jianxin Yang, Le Yu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Qwen3-Omni is the first single multimodal model to maintain state-of-the-art performance across text, image, audio, and video without degradation relative to single-modal counterparts.\n  2. The model adopts a Thinker-Talker Mixture-of-Experts architecture that unifies perception and generation across text, images, audio, and video to yield fluent text and natural real-time speech.\n  3. It replaces the Whisper audio encoder with an Audio Transformer encoder trained from scratch on 20 million hours of supervised audio to yield stronger general-purpose audio representations.\n  4. A multi-codebook autoregressive scheme with a multi-token prediction module is introduced for speech generation, replacing block-wise diffusion with a lightweight causal ConvNet.\n  5. The system supports text interaction in 119 languages, speech understanding in 19 languages, and speech generation in 10 languages.\n  6. A Time-aligned Multimodal Rotary Position Embedding interleaves rotary angles across temporal, height, and width dimensions to enhance long-range dependency modeling for multimodal streams.\n  7. A Thinking model is introduced to explicitly reason over inputs from any modality, including audio-video and audio-only scenarios.\n  8. Qwen3-Omni-30B-A3B-Captioner is fine-tuned to produce detailed, low-hallucination captions for arbitrary audio inputs to address the lack of general-purpose audio captioning models.\n  9. The model achieves a theoretical end-to-end first-packet latency of 234 ms in cold-start settings through chunked prefilling and streaming multi-codebook codec generation.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/对话型, LALM/潜在表示, LALM/对话型-并行生成, TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b6357e8026c0f08c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# TurnGuide: Enhancing Meaningful Full Duplex Spoken Interactions via Dynamic Turn-Level Text-Speech Interleaving\narXiv: 2508.07375\nAuthors: Wenqian Cui, Lei Zhu, Xiaohui Li, Zhihan Guo, Haoli Bai, Lu Hou, Irwin King\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: dialogue_system\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose TurnGuide, a novel text-speech interleaved generation approach for end-to-end full-duplex speech language models grounded in natural speech data.\n  2. We introduce a dynamic turn segmentation framework to address the insertion timing and length challenges of integrating text into double-channel dialogues.\n  3. We introduce a text-guided dialogue modeling framework that interleaves text and speech generation at the turn level to preserve natural acoustic flow.\n  4. We demonstrate through extensive experiments that TurnGuide significantly improves the semantic coherence of generated speech and achieves state-of-the-art performance on turn-taking events.\n\nTags: LALM/对话型-交错标记, LALM/对话型-纯语音, Agent/全双工", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "76c6e56c-0afb-448b-9686-315b09104bea", "uuid": "618cf3ae-0575-49a7-9387-ac31c5ca51f0", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T16:15:10.893Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# TurnGuide: Enhancing Meaningful Full Duplex Spoken Interactions via Dynamic Turn-Level Text-Speech Interleaving\narXiv: 2508.07375\nAuthors: Wenqian Cui, Lei Zhu, Xiaohui Li, Zhihan Guo, Haoli Bai, Lu Hou, Irwin King\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: dialogue_system\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose TurnGuide, a novel text-speech interleaved generation approach for end-to-end full-duplex speech language models grounded in natural speech data.\n  2. We introduce a dynamic turn segmentation framework to address the insertion timing and length challenges of integrating text into double-channel dialogues.\n  3. We introduce a text-guided dialogue modeling framework that interleaves text and speech generation at the turn level to preserve natural acoustic flow.\n  4. We demonstrate through extensive experiments that TurnGuide significantly improves the semantic coherence of generated speech and achieves state-of-the-art performance on turn-taking events.\n\nTags: LALM/对话型-交错标记, LALM/对话型-纯语音, Agent/全双工", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
