{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b27ffdc0a01e9a71", "type": "tool_result", "content": "2512.19090\n===\n# JoyVoice: Long-Context Conditioning for Anthropomorphic Multi-Speaker Conversational Synthesis\narXiv: 2512.19090\nAuthors: Fan Yu, Tao Wang, You Wu, Lin Zhu, Wei Deng, Weisheng Han, Wenchao Wang, Lin Hu, Xiangyu Liang, Xiaodong He, Yankun Huang, Yu Gu, Yuan Liu, Yuxuan Wang, Zhangyu Xiao, Ziteng Wang, Boya Dong, Feng Dang, Jinming Chen, Jingdong Li, Jun Wang, Yechen Jin, Yuan Zhang, Zhengyan Sheng, Xin Wang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Integrated End-to-End Architecture: We propose a unified framework where AR-Transformer hidden states directly condition a global causal DiT, ensuring seamless optimization and superior multi-speaker synthesis.\n  2. High-Efficiency MM-Tokenizer: We introduce a tokenizer operating at 25Hz & 12.5 Hz that balances semantic understanding and acoustic reconstruction through multi-task losses.\n  3. Robustness without Normalization: By leveraging large-scale data perturbation and synthetic generation, JoyVoice reduces dependency on text normalization modules while maximizing stability.\n  4. SOTA Performance: JoyVoice achieves state-of-the-art results on the Seed-TTS-Eval Benchmark and complex conversational voice cloning tasks, surpassing existing baselines in prosody, consistency, and similarity.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-长时间, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "76c6e56c-0afb-448b-9686-315b09104bea", "uuid": "2c84ff71-7765-47b7-8ff0-96c0e7e3bb8a", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T16:15:47.086Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "2512.19090\n===\n# JoyVoice: Long-Context Conditioning for Anthropomorphic Multi-Speaker Conversational Synthesis\narXiv: 2512.19090\nAuthors: Fan Yu, Tao Wang, You Wu, Lin Zhu, Wei Deng, Weisheng Han, Wenchao Wang, Lin Hu, Xiangyu Liang, Xiaodong He, Yankun Huang, Yu Gu, Yuan Liu, Yuxuan Wang, Zhangyu Xiao, Ziteng Wang, Boya Dong, Feng Dang, Jinming Chen, Jingdong Li, Jun Wang, Yechen Jin, Yuan Zhang, Zhengyan Sheng, Xin Wang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Integrated End-to-End Architecture: We propose a unified framework where AR-Transformer hidden states directly condition a global causal DiT, ensuring seamless optimization and superior multi-speaker synthesis.\n  2. High-Efficiency MM-Tokenizer: We introduce a tokenizer operating at 25Hz & 12.5 Hz that balances semantic understanding and acoustic reconstruction through multi-task losses.\n  3. Robustness without Normalization: By leveraging large-scale data perturbation and synthetic generation, JoyVoice reduces dependency on text normalization modules while maximizing stability.\n  4. SOTA Performance: JoyVoice achieves state-of-the-art results on the Seed-TTS-Eval Benchmark and complex conversational voice cloning tasks, surpassing existing baselines in prosody, consistency, and similarity.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-长时间, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
